      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey quick question, im taking the eurostar from st pancras to paris next week and i have a couple of massive suitcases. what are the actual weight and size limits for luggage? also when do i really need to be there to check in?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Eurostar from St Pancras to Paris, a great way to travel. You'll be glad to know that the luggage size and weight limits are quite reasonable, but you should still be mindful of them to avoid any issues. The maximum weight limit for checked luggage is 23kg (50lbs), and the maximum size is 158cm (62 inches) in length, 119cm (47 inches) in width, and 27cm (11 inches) in height. It's a bit like a big, sturdy box, but not as cumbersome as a giant, lumbering troll's luggage.\n\nAs for checking in, it's recommended to arrive at least 30 minutes before your train departs. However, if you have a lot of luggage, you may want to consider checking in online or at a self-service kiosk to save time. Just be aware that if you have too much luggage, you might need to pay an extra fee, which is a bit like a goblin's \"toll\" for carrying too much treasure.\n\nIf you're planning to check in at the airport, you can usually find the Eurostar check-in desks around 1-2 hours before your train departs. Just look for the signs that",
